+    /// A WebUI surface composited onto a rectangle in the world -- a television.
+    ///
+    /// The rectangle is authored in the *prop's* local frame rather than read
+    /// from its geometry, and that is a constraint of this engine rather than a
+    /// preference: a prop's mesh cannot be redirected after its components are
+    /// attached, so the props this can be attached to are Open77-owned hosts
+    /// whose component graph is baked at asset-build time. Reading a screen
+    /// rectangle back out of one of those would mean resolving a submesh by name
+    /// per television, and a prop that renamed it would move the screen
+    /// silently. Authored data cannot silently disagree with itself.
+    ///
+    /// `prop` and `surface` are decimal strings in Lua, because a 64-bit handle
+    /// loses precision in a Lua number; the same convention markers, props and
